{
  "id": "Compound::DB00383 - Gene::1128",
  "verbalization": "Oxyphencyclimine is likely to interact with Chrm1 through a mechanism involving G-protein coupled receptors. The evidence suggests that Oxyphencyclimine binds to Chrm2 or Chrm3, which are both involved in G-protein coupled acetylcholine or neurotransmitter receptor activities. These receptors are then participated in by Chrm1, indicating a potential functional link between Oxyphencyclimine and Chrm1. The overlapping roles of Chrm2 and Chrm3 in activating G-protein coupled receptor activity suggest that Oxyphencyclimine may influence Chrm1 through these receptors, possibly modulating signaling pathways that are critical for receptor function. The consistent involvement of G-protein coupled receptor activity in the pathways of both Chrm2 and Chrm3 supports the hypothesis that Oxyphencyclimine exerts its effects on Chrm1 via these receptors, though the exact mechanism of interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
